{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling","id":1055953,"title":"Legendary/Epic Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-27T19:42:09-08:00","id":1055953,"title":"Legendary/Epic Changeling","content":"According to MachineIV and Rose Bailey the Changeling 2E line end at the <i>Hunter Chronicle</i>, for now. I am hoping that they can be convinced to continue the Changeling line with a Changeling crossover book and an Epic Changeling chronicle. I would really like to see an epic changeling chronicle that reinterprets major mythology heroes and villains, as well as famous people as wyrd 10 Changelings or True Fae. To give some ideas, here are Ichabod Crane and Edgar Allen Poe reinterpreted as Changelings of the Autumn Court. <br /> <b><i>Edgar Allen Poe</i></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">A character I think would be interesting to introduce in the <i>Huntsmen Chronicles</i> is Edgar Allen Poe as a Fairest Author and the most powerful Autumn Court monarch in the Southern United States. Poes\u2019 story of becoming a changeling is an interesting one, because he started out as fae-touched. When his wife Eleanor(Virginia Eliza Clemm Poe) died of Tuberculosis, Poe fell into despair and considered suicide. On the night he contemplated death, he was visited a raven (Actually a huntsman for a True Fae known as <i>The Red Death</i>). The Raven revealed it\u2019s true nature and the revelation that Virginia Eliza Clemm Poe i.e. Leanor was still alive. She had been given to one of the Great Sea Kings by Poe\u2019s enemy Rufus Griswold. <i>The Raven</i> and <i>The Red Death</i> promised to help him retrieve his wife. In exchange, he would write about his experiences in the Hedge and Arcadia. A fetch was left back in Bronx, New York who would copy the stories Poe sent him. During his travel in Arcadia, he writes <i>The Raven, Fairy-Land, The Tell Tale Heart, The Gold Bug, Elizabeth, Mask of the Red Death, the Black Cat, and Cask of Armontollio.</i> When he came to the Kingdom by the Sea, he used his skill in story telling to defeat huntsmen sent after him, outwit the Sea King, and rescue his bride. When he finally returned to the mortal realm, his fetch had died a strange and most tragic death. Much to Poe\u2019s cold amusement, the efforts of Rufus Griswold to destroy his reputation led to his literary infamy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Because of his experience, knowledge, and skill in the occult, Poe joined the Autumn Court and became one of the most powerful monarchs in the Southern U.S.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Poe\u2019s Wife Eleanor is a darkling Waterborn. At first I wanted her to be a Banshee. However, because Poe\u2019s poem, <i>The Raven</i>, connects her to death to the sea. It therefore made sense to me that her kith would be tied to water.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Ichabod Crane</i></b></span><br /> <br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">In 1790, in Tarry Town, New York, there was a school teacher named Ichabod Crane. Tall, lean, and lanky, he looked like a goofy scarecrow. Although he is resented by much of the rough country men of the town, he is a favorite of the ladies. One day, he falls in love with eighteen year old, Katrina Van Tassel, who is a daughter of the wealthy Baltus Van Tassel. Unfortunately, she is also courted by Abraham &quot;Brom Bones&quot; Van Blunt, a rowdy and bully, but popular the towns people for &quot;being one of them.&quot; Blunt first tries to drive Crane away by playing cruel pranks on him and spreading the rumor that Crane wants to marry Katrina to get a hold of the Van Tassel's wealth. Much to Blunt's frustration, Katrina is attracted more to the cultured and educated Ichabod Crane. One day, a stranger payed a visit to Blunt. If he can lead Ichabod Crane to Sleepy Hollow, Crane will be never be seen again. Brunt tells Crane that Baltus Van Tassel want to talk to Crane about marrying his daughter. Along the way, he passes through sleepy hollow, where a True Fae, the headless horseman, snatches him up, and Ichabod is never seen in the two again. Afterward, through the coercion of the towns people and the commands of her father, Katrina Van Tassel marries Abraham Blunt. Blunt eventually meets Washington Irving and tells him a mudslinging version of what what happened to Ichabod Crane (<i>Which Became the Tale of Sleepy Hollow)</i> to ruin Ichabod Crane's reputation. Ironically, Blunt eventually grows tired of her and gives her to the Headless Horseman, too.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Over a century later, (in the year 1910) , two darklings, one male and one female come out of the hedge gate to Sleepy Hollow. They join the Autumn Court with the male eventually joining the Scarecrow Ministry and becomes one of its most infamous members. The tale he most often uses is that of <i>Sleepy Hollow.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T20:22:44-08:00","id":1055961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling#post1055953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to MachineIV and Rose Bailey the Changeling 2E line end at the <i>Hunter Chronicle</i>, for now. I am hoping that they can be convinced to continue the Changeling line with a Changeling crossover book and an Epic Changeling chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misunderstood me. The line doesn't <i>end</i> at that point, it's that we haven't entered active production on the supplements. Supplements are definitely on the schedule!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T20:26:48-08:00","id":1055963,"title":"","content":"Excellent<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Is there discussion of doing an Epic Changeling sourcebook?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T21:51:01-08:00","id":1055988,"title":"","content":"As far as I can tell, there was plan for a The Hedge book next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T22:02:40-08:00","id":1055990,"title":"","content":"Yes, and then a <i>Huntsmen Chronicle</i>, but I am hoping that there is at least discussions of ideas for other books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T22:18:03-08:00","id":1055994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1055990#post1055990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and then a <i>Huntsmen Chronicle</i>, but I am hoping that there is at least discussions of ideas for other books.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Huntsmen Chronicle is part of the corebook, not a seperate affair. Thus the grand tradition of Second Edition continues.(See the Strix Chronicle, the Idigam Chronicle, the Fallen World Chronicle, the Firestorm Chronicle, and the Slasher Chronicle for more should you care).<br /> <br /> The Hedge is confirmed as a supplement. Are there other books after that?<br /> <br /> *glances down at his filing cabinet*<br /> <br /> Anyways, sooner or later, a revisitation of legendary changelings seems, to me anyways, an inevitability, but that's just me and I legitimately have no idea on the actuality of that. Such beings draw stories in around themselves anyways. In the meantime, Equinox Road still exists.<br /> &quot;<br /> (Since I feel like there's at least the one person who might ask, no, the Tuatha are shelved, I am not pitching that idea ever.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T18:09:34-08:00","id":1056399,"title":"","content":"Would anyone like to further develop the story of these characters as wyrd 10 changelings?<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><b>Cu Chulainn</b> as 1d4chan\u2019s Berserker kith of the Oger seeming. A member of the Summer Court, who is legendary for his rage. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><b>Queen Medb of Ireland</b> as a Fairest Soldier. Originally a Queen of the Summer Court, as her wyrd and legend rose, she eventually became worshipped as a goddess by the Irish Tribes.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><b>King Arthur</b> as a Draconic Fairest and Monarch of the Summer Court in Britain and Wales. He sleeps until the times of Britains\u2019 greatest dangers.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><b>Merlin</b> as a Oracle/Minstrel Dual Kith. I can see him starting out as having the wizened seeming, but losing it in order to escape from the tree Nimue trapped him in.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T20:03:07-08:00","id":1056432,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#393A39\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">In an epic Changeling book, I really think it should explore the relationship between Vasilisa the Beautiful and Baba Yaga. Because these characters have already been used in Classic World of Darkness as vampires, I want to give them a unique twist. In researching the slavic goddess, <i>Morena,</i> I was intrigued to learn that some legends claim that Baba Yaga is just one of Morena\u2019s guises. This has led to the idea making Morena a True Fae and Baba Yaga one of her actors (though she could also be one on Morena\u2019s Huntsmen). Koshchei the Deathless could be a darkling loyalist the serves Morena, since Eastern Slavs have legends of him being her husband. If Baba Yaga is one of Morena\u2019s actor\u2019s, then her Huntsmen are the White(Day), Red (Sun), and Black(Night) riders that serve her.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#393A39\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">As for Vasilisa\u2026I see her as a Flame Siren with the Grimm seeming. She doesn\u2019t have the fairest seeming, since she didn\u2019t heroically rescue anyone, but follow the orders of Baba Yaga and her doll. So her doll(which is implied to contain the soul of her mother) could be a manikin fairest or wizened depending on whether you want to emphasize her being a heroic character who saved her daughter or as a wizened who used her ingenuity to complete the tasks Baba Yaga set for Vasilisa; clean Baba\u2019s house and yard, wash her laundry, and cook her meal. </span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T21:25:06-08:00","id":1056468,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#393A39\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I forgot to mention that is some versions of the myth of Vasilisa and Baba Yaga, after returning home (and killing her step family) Vasilisa marries a Tsar. I can see her becoming a a Queen at one of the most influential courts in Russia and Eastern Europe.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T23:42:23-08:00","id":1056506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1056432#post1056432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In an epic Changeling book, I really think it should explore the relationship between Vasilisa the Beautiful and Baba Yaga. Because these characters have already been used in Classic World of Darkness as vampires, I want to give them a unique twist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Idk, one of the good things about CofD is that it's not &quot;this the setting, here are the big NPC's&quot;. There's a reason the nWoD stuff about dracula isn't solid info on him, just many theories and stories, and the closet thing to a statblock of him is a poser (though I wouldn't say that to his face).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:40:42-08:00","id":1056843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1056506#post1056506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idk, one of the good things about CofD is that it's not &quot;this the setting, here are the big NPC's&quot;. There's a reason the nWoD stuff about dracula isn't solid info on him, just many theories and stories, and the closet thing to a statblock of him is a poser (though I wouldn't say that to his face).</div> </div> </div> </div>What you say is true, but even in new world of darkness, they usually give you a detailed character description to play them as allies or enemies. Plus I think it would be fun to explore the myths and legends connected to some of these characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:31:49-08:00","id":1056873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1056843#post1056843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you say is true, but even in new world of darkness, they usually give you a detailed character description to play them as allies or enemies. Plus I think it would be fun to explore the myths and legends connected to some of these characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a whole world of them to visit, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:37:54-08:00","id":1056876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1056843#post1056843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you say is true, but even in new world of darkness, they usually give you a detailed character description to play them as allies or enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really....? Closest I can see to that is some NPC's in night horrors books, but none of those are characters from myth like what your suggesting here. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus I think it would be fun to explore the myths and legends connected to some of these characters. </div> </div> </div>Only way I could see this working is discussing themes of those legends in Hunting Grounds chapters, like if you have a russian hunting ground, the courts might be baba yaga based. Which isn't really what your asking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T18:11:50-08:00","id":1056905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1056873#post1056873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a whole world of them to visit, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could focus on the ones from Celtic and Scandinavian sources, first. Then depending on how popular those character are, expand into other mythologies.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Not really....? Closest I can see to that is some NPC's in night horrors books, but none of those are characters from myth like what your suggesting here.</span></span></span></i><br /> <br /> I remember a Forsaken book (Can't remember it's title, sorry<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) in which it introduced Sitting Bull as a Pure Tribe Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> Only way I could see this working is discussing themes of those legends in Hunting Grounds chapters, like if you have a russian hunting ground, the courts might be baba yaga based. Which isn't really what your asking for.<br /> <br /> To me, If you are going to play a Epic changeling(wyrd 10) Changeling, my feeling is you should be pretty close to end game and dealing with world ending, Ragnarok/Gehenna level scenarios, like a full fledged invasion of Earth by the True Fae. Or at least playing the game as high fantasy, which means encountering a lot of epic characters. Though there are probably other ways to play it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T18:14:06-08:00","id":1056906,"title":"","content":"To be more specific, I meant I think an Epic changeling game should be more global than a typical Changeling game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T18:17:43-08:00","id":1056911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1056905#post1056905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could focus on the ones from Celtic and Scandinavian sources, first. Then depending on how popular those character are, expand into other mythologies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would rather do, I 'unno, Mexican and Indian first. Maybe more of the varying Polynesian myths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T18:39:26-08:00","id":1056920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1056905#post1056905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember a Forsaken book (Can't remember it's title, sorry<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) in which it introduced Sitting Bull as a Pure Tribe Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot say that I remember that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me, If you are going to play a Epic changeling(wyrd 10) Changeling, my feeling is you should be pretty close to end game and dealing with world ending, Ragnarok/Gehenna level scenarios, like a full fledged invasion of Earth by the True Fae. </div> </div> </div>End of the world-scale scenarios are more a WoD thing than a CofD thing. Though I can see shards like that in a Changeling Storyteller's Guide like Demon had.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or at least playing the game as high fantasy, which means encountering a lot of epic characters. </div> </div> </div>Considering most high fantasy is in non-earth settings and lack the appearance of &quot;real-world mythic characters&quot;. I find this a rather surprising perspective. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">To be more specific, I meant I think an Epic changeling game should be more global than a typical Changeling game.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> That seems sort of opposite to wanting information on &quot;tying specific individuals and legends into changeling&quot; which are in &quot;specific regions of the world&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T19:05:25-08:00","id":1056931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1056911#post1056911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would rather do, I 'unno, Mexican and Indian first. Maybe more of the varying Polynesian myths.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could also start with some of our most popular fairytales ( King Arthur, Robin Hood, Red Riding Hood, Snow White, The Pied Piper of Hamlin) and some American folktales like Jack O'Shadows. The Mexican, Indian, and Polynesian myths could be explored in an International Changeling book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T19:12:52-08:00","id":1056933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1056920#post1056920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [/FONT]<br /> That seems sort of opposite to wanting information on &quot;tying specific individuals and legends into changeling&quot; which are in &quot;specific regions of the world&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, I bring it up, because I don't think an Epic changeling book should focus on character backgrounds of wyrd 10 Changelings and True Fae. I think there should be a section in the book describing these legendary Changelings and how can used in either &quot;specific regional stories&quot; or &quot;epic campaigns&quot;. The other sections should focus on End of the World Scenarios, Stats for True Fae, so you can fight and even kill them, how to potentially set up a cult that worships you, maybe level 6 through 10 contracts, or how you could eventually <i>evolve </i>into something greater than a True Fae or even the God-Machine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T20:09:37-08:00","id":1056955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1056931#post1056931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could also start with some of our most popular fairytales ( King Arthur, Robin Hood, Red Riding Hood, Snow White, The Pied Piper of Hamlin) and some American folktales like Jack O'Shadows. The Mexican, Indian, and Polynesian myths could be explored in an International Changeling book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or I could just do more, less known stories that mean more to non-Europeans.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I need a writing count for that first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T20:29:43-08:00","id":1056962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1056955#post1056955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or I could just do more, less known stories that mean more to non-Europeans.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I need a writing count for that first.</div> </div> </div> </div>True<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Would you consider exploring <b><i>Journey to the West</i></b>? It is one of my favorite non-European legends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T20:30:40-08:00","id":1056965,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#393A39\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Snow White:</span></i></b><br /> <br /> Here\u2019s my reinterpretation of Snow White as a changeling. Her step-mother is a fae touched loyalist who is given a magic mirror by her True Fae master for her services to him (which include bringing her kingdom under the True Fae\u2019s thrall). When she learns that Snow White is more beautiful than her, in a jealous rage, the Queen asks the True Fae to send a huntsman to kill Snow White, which he does. But he also double crosses his queen-servant by helping Snow White escape to the Hedge. The Huntsman first stalks Snow White as a woodsman to cut out her heart, a comb seller with a poisoned comb, and then as an old crone who tries to poison her with hobgoblin fruit. Snow White keeps the huntsmen at bay, first by sacrificing the seven dwarves to him (which earns her the darkling seeming) and then eating the part of the hobgoblin fruit that does not kill her, but puts her in a deathlike trance. The True Fae is so impressed by her cunning and ruthlessness that takes the role of a prince and kisses her to awaken her from the spell she is under. The True Fae (Still in the guise of a prince) invites Snow Whites\u2019 step-mother to a banquet. When she arrives, Snow White reveals herself and tortures her step-mother to death by forcing her to dance in red hot iron shoes. The True-Fae prince is deeply moved by her beauty; for her skin is white as snow, her lips as red as blood, and has a heart as black as coal. He takes her to his realm, where she acts as his fury, punishing anyone who fails or disappoints him. As is common with the True Fae, he began growing tired of her. Sensing this, Snow White fled his kingdom and returned to her old kingdom, which had become the Holy-Roman Empire.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#393A39\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Snow White is a Fury (Deionscribe\u2019s kith) of the Darkling seeming. She is so beautiful, however, she is often mistaken for being of the Fairest seeming. She uses the fairytales of Snow White to further enhance this belief. Her incredible beauty comes from possessing two merits, <i>Enchanting</i> and <i>Vanity</i>.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Enchanting(2 to 3 dots)</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>Striking looks, wyrd 6</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Effect:</b> Your Looks are beyond striking, you are the very incarnation of beauty and eroticism. Or you are the personification of ideal heroism from which villains cringe in terror and the common folk look at in awe. In the two dot version of this merit, your character automatically get 4 dots in striking looks and can buy dots in striking looks up to their wyrd. At three dots, with the exception of wound penalties, you character is immune to all penalties on appearance (they don\u2019t have bad B.O., they don\u2019t need to spend hours in from of the mirror grooming themselves, and they can walk though a puddle of mud and not get a speck of dirt on their clothes or shoes).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i>Note: If your character has the fairest seeming, they don\u2019t need striking looks to purchase this merit. If the fairest character does not have striking looks, upon purchasing this merit, they automatically gain the two dot version of striking looks. If the fairest already has the striking looks, they gain twice the normal limit.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b><i>Drawback:</i></b> the character is extremely memorable. all other characters gain two dice to notice and recall the character.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Vanity(3 dots)</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b><i>Prerequisite:</i></b> Enchanting Beauty, wyrd 10</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b><i>Effect: </i></b>Your beauty is now alien and monstrous. Mortals will fall instantly in love (or at least lust) or kill themselves, knowing that they will never be able to match/ compare. When dealing with mortals/human all difficulties in presence and relevant skill drop to zero. If the character is a changeling, if their will power does not match the presence + skill roll, must spend a dot of glamor to try to resist it. If the character with this merit succeeds in their roll, they can cause <i>TWO </i>conditions. If the changeling is a seducer, they can cause the swoon and wanton conditions or the swoon and infatuated conditions. Or they can cause the inspired and Steadfast condition.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T22:08:11-08:00","id":1056980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1056911#post1056911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would rather do, I 'unno, Mexican and Indian first. Maybe more of the varying Polynesian myths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually pretty interested in this. I would like to also see kiths specific to these legends, as well as a description of what the hedge in these regions might look like<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T20:10:33-08:00","id":1057419,"title":"","content":"I think that a changeling book that focused on epic/legendary changelings would be a good place to explore the dark realities behind some of our favorite folk heroes. For example, contrary to the popular myth of Robin Hood being a heroic character who stole from the rich who gave to the poor, the real Robin Hood was a well born cut-throat who stole from everyone and gave to himself.<br /> <br /> As such, I would make him a darkling larcenist.<br /> <br /> And their was nothing charming about the real pied piper of hamlin who was a psychopath and pederast. He kidnapped hundreds of village children and left the remains of their corpses floating down rivers. I would make him a darkling Thrusser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T20:12:58-08:00","id":1057420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1056962#post1056962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Would you consider exploring <b><i>Journey to the West</i></b>? It is one of my favorite non-European legends.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also like the Changeling scenario in Japan developed. As an anime/manga fan, i would like to see one True Fae whose realm in Arcadia and changelings were based on anime/manga. I would also like to see a freehold similar to Touhou, were changelings lived and interacted with mages, shape shifters, heists, and beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T05:19:14-08:00","id":1057542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1055961#post1055961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you misunderstood me. The line doesn't <i>end</i> at that point, it's that we haven't entered active production on the supplements. Supplements are definitely on the schedule!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> WHEW!<br /> <br /> My heart stopped for a hot second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T05:25:08-08:00","id":1057544,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, Hatter, while you have some interesting ideas here, they don't match my conception of the game.<br /> <br /> That said, I think it would be cool to see a Shards or fan supplement that does Changeling-by-way-of-Fables. They have a lot of similar themes, and I could see it mechanically adapting fairly well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T08:47:52-08:00","id":1057613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1057419#post1057419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that a changeling book that focused on epic/legendary changelings would be a good place to explore the dark realities behind some of our favorite folk heroes. For example, contrary to the popular myth of Robin Hood being a heroic character who stole from the rich who gave to the poor, the real Robin Hood was a well born cut-throat who stole from everyone and gave to himself.<br /> <br /> As such, I would make him a darkling larcenist.<br /> <br /> And their was nothing charming about the real pied piper of hamlin who was a psychopath and pederast. He kidnapped hundreds of village children and left the remains of their corpses floating down rivers. I would make him a darkling Thrusser.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to see your sources on those.<br /> <br /> One thing I'd consider when coming up with these would be whether it needs to be a specific figure, or whether it would work well as a parallel to said figure. For example, think of a lot of the characters from the Night Horrors book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T19:04:42-08:00","id":1057872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1057544#post1057544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, Hatter, while you have some interesting ideas here, they don't match my conception of the game.<br /> <br /> That said, I think it would be cool to see a Shards or fan supplement that does Changeling-by-way-of-Fables. They have a lot of similar themes, and I could see it mechanically adapting fairly well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Changeling: the Lost 2e will be different enough from 1e, that several of the idea I profess are possible. For example. Changelings in 2e can now, potentially live forever (either through the long of days merit or reaching wyrd 10). Also, obtaining wyrd 10 does not automatically mean that your clarity drops to zero and you get your happy ass back to Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T19:06:04-08:00","id":1057873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1057613#post1057613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would love to see your sources on those.<br /> <br /> One thing I'd consider when coming up with these would be whether it needs to be a specific figure, or whether it would work well as a parallel to said figure. For example, think of a lot of the characters from the Night Horrors book.</div> </div> </div> </div>One source was William Manchester's <b><i>A World Lit only by Fire</i></b>, which explores life during the Renaissance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","user":"Madhatter","date":". 03-03-2017, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T19:39:18-08:00","id":1057888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1057613#post1057613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing I'd consider when coming up with these would be whether it needs to be a specific figure, or whether it would work well as a parallel to said figure. For example, think of a lot of the characters from the Night Horrors book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the wyrd 10 characters all have to be in one book, but can be put in books that share a theme associated with them. For example, when Changeling 1e came out, I felt that the concept of the horror of being an adult trapped in a child's body would work well in a Changeling setting. This belief was further enhanced by the character of Wild Sam. A Changeling book that focused on Changeling trapped in the form/stage of a child could be used to introduce wyrd 10 changelings like, Peter Pan, Alice Liddell( Adventures in Wonderland/Through the Looking Glass), Gerda and Kai( The Snow Queen), and even Oliver Twist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T06:13:43-08:00","id":1058016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1057873#post1057873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One source was William Manchester's <b><i>A World Lit only by Fire</i></b>, which explores life during the Renaissance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I will need to look into that when I get the chance. Everything I've read previously seemed to indicate that the origins of these tales were uncertain as far as actual historical figures were concerned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T14:44:48-08:00","id":1058156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1057888#post1057888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> when Changeling 1e came out, I felt that the concept of the horror of being an adult trapped in a child's body would work well in a Changeling setting. This belief was further enhanced by the character of Wild Sam. A Changeling book that focused on Changeling trapped in the form/stage of a child could be used to introduce wyrd 10 changelings like, Peter Pan, Alice Liddell( Adventures in Wonderland/Through the Looking Glass), Gerda and Kai( The Snow Queen), and even Oliver Twist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see a lot of people stating that this kind of character would be extremely difficult or nearly impossible to play.<br /> <br /> These are some examples that can be really good sources of inspiration. These include..<br /> Scottie Young's <b><i>I Hate Fairyland</i></b><br /> Soman Chainaini's <b><i>School For Good and Evil </i></b> trilogy.<br /> Stephen King's <b><i>It</i></b><br /> <br /> plus, the classics<br /> <br /> <i>Peter Pan</i><br /> Lewis Carroll's <b><i>Alice in Wonderland </i></b> and <b><i>Through the Looking Glass.</i></b><br /> <br /> and the original <b><i>Dorothy </i></b>series<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T18:15:08-08:00","id":1058231,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">One of the most popular mysteries is the identity and disappearance of Jack the Ripper. What most people don\u2019t know is that one of the Gentry was so impressed with his work, that she spirited him away to her realm in Arcadia. There, he acted as her loyalist-huntsmen and torturer who tracked down and tortured those changelings who tried top escape her. One day, however, he lost her patronage after a motley of changelings escaped from him. He fled her wrath back to London. Ironically, when the song <i>Jack the Ripper is Dead</i> was becoming popular. He joined both the Autumn Court and is one of the most evil members of the Ministry of the Scarecrow. He promotes the urban legend of Jack the Ripper through horrifying murders and making people disappear. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Jack is a dual kith Fury/Razorhand of the darkling seeming.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","user":"Madhatter","date":". 03-05-2017, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T19:41:11-08:00","id":1058744,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">In Changeling 1e\u2019s description of the beast seeming, I really liked the unique twist in the <i>Beauty and the Beast</i> story they gave where kissing the Beast True Fae caused Beauty to become a beast. So I think it would be really interesting to introduce such a character in Changeling 2e. I think White Oak Dragon\u2019s Cursed One Kith Would work well with such a character and be very effective when combined with the Beast seeming.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Does anyone have ideas for the back story of such a character?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T20:44:23-08:00","id":1058767,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><i>Jack of the Lantern</i></b> called Stingy Jack or Drunk Jack in his mortal life was an Irish black smith in Ireland several centuries ago, known for his deceitfulness and cunning. One day, one of the Gentry tried to steal Jack away to his realm in Arcadia. No one is sure how he did it, but Jack convinced the True Fae to take him to a local pub and pay for his drink. When the Gentry tried to pay by turning himself into a gold coin, Jack stuck True Fae in his pocket which contained a bar of cold iron. Unable to move, Jack forced him to never bother him again for eternity. Word of one of their own being deceived by a mortal spread like wild fire throughout all the realms in Arcadia and Jack found himself challenged again and again, until one of the True Fae was able to defeat him and whisk him away to Arcadia. One hundred years later, Jack emerged from Arcadia, but with a unique twist. He was barred from never stepping foot in the lands of the Gentry again. He eventually joined the Autumn Court, but was banished from Freehold to Freehold, because of all the chaos and mischief he created. This meshes well with a minor frailty he gained at wyrd 7 which forbids him from entering foot in place of civilization like a city of freehold. Jack now wanders though the wilderness and hedge of Western Europe and North America. He has joined the Magi of the Guilded Thorn and is one of its most experienced members. Unfortunately, he is also known to intermingle with Racketeers and is justly as likely to sell out a Changeling or Fae-Touched as well as help them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Although the Darkling seeming would better suit Jack, for some unknown reason he has the Wizened seeming. He has the Barrister/Farwalker dual kith.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T15:03:12-08:00","id":1059224,"title":"","content":"Honestly, of all the 1e books that I wouldn't mind a literal rehash/update directly for, the tier 4 books (equinox road, imperial mysteries) take the cake. I loved how Seeming and Kitsch evolved with Wyrd, but because of some changes in 2e, I think advanced changelings are a good topic to cover. More immortals isn't necessarily a bad thing. I don't know if I'd dig a big list of famous immortal changeling superfolk from legend (the true fae will break the fourth wall, find that list, and hunt them down for sport like dragons), but I don't think an example (like the stated out Inheritors, in Beast) is a bad idea.<br /> <br /> However, I think as writers, Arc and the boss would not likely use someone like Peter Pan or Dorothy because they wouldn't want to cement exactly who or what such legends are. Stating out Peter as a wyrd 10 changeling or Baba Yaga as a True Fae will affect how some people use those beings in game. Which is bad, because in my last game Pan was changeling and Baba was true fae, but in my current game, Pan is true fae and Baba is a Primordial begotten with strong family ties to mages, fae, and one shuanksen that shares an ex lover with her. Now, knowing the creative geniuses behind the changeling game line, they would be able to pull off a pseudo-legendary character that MIGHT be the source of the legend, or might be just one of the near extinct Grimms stealing the plot, or a changeling made by a true fae in its own image. Either way, unless that changeling was explicitly a Grimm, or meant to become a solid character fixture like the npcs of Mummy, if they DO make example wyrd 10 changeling, Id bet they will be original characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T16:05:23-08:00","id":1059257,"title":"","content":"It doesn't have to be a big list of wyrd 10 changes. The legendary Fae could be be examples of how to play variations of different types of immortals you can play. Like a lost boy, i.e. a changeling stuck in the form of a child, but have the minds of adults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T16:15:41-08:00","id":1059263,"title":"","content":"While I am on the subject of playing a Lost Boy. Here are some more sources of inspiration for playing such a character.<br /> <br /> For those of you who read manga, I recommend reading the first few Detective Conan for playing such a character. Also there is a very, very, very obscure manga called <b><i>Chairudo</i></b> that I think that i think gives a good example for playing such a character. You should be able to find them on manga escalation sites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T20:55:42-08:00","id":1059331,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><i>The Snow Queen: </i></b>Thousands of years ago, One of the True Fae made a mirror that would show only the ugliness in the world. He and several other members of the Gentry flew high into the mortal sky, hoping to use the mirror to warp the God-machine and maybe even destroy it. However, the higher they took it, the heavier the mirror became until it fell from their hands and shattered into grains of sand entering the eyes of humanity, freezing their hearts and causing them to see only the ugliness and evil in the world. Many years later, they flew into the eyes of a young boy name Kai, who became mean and cruel. He began to bully and torment his childhood friend, Gerda. The only beauty he could see was in the snowflakes. Seeing his admiration for the cold, a True Fae known as the Snow Queen, spirited him away to her realm of ice and snow in Arcadia. She made Kai forget about his mortal family and his town believe that he had drowned in the river. Grieving, Gerda goes to the River and offers her new red shoes. The River does not take the shoes and tells Gerda that Kai was spirited into Arcadia, opening a path into the Hedge. While traveling along one of the Trods, she encounters one of the Gentry who removes Gerda\u2019s memory of Kai and her life on Earth. She spends many years in the Gentry\u2019s Garden of Eternal Summer makes her remember Kai, again. She escapes her keepers realm and continues her quest for Kai. Her keeper tries to entice Gerda back to her realm using a magical castle with a Kai look alike and beautiful clothes. Finally, she sends a group of racketeers to recapture Gerda, but she comes a reindeer to escape them. Finally, Gerda reaches the Snow Queen\u2019s realm. The Snow Queen tries to stop her with her snow bees, whose stings leave a man frozen and dead. However, using a token stolen from her Keepers realm, she summons and angel or fire and sunlight thet kills the snow bees. Gerda enters the Snow Queens castle and finds Kai frozen deep in the Snow Queens mirror of reason. He seems dead whole trying to solve the puzzle that the Snow Queen gave him to solve, forgotten as she searches for new toys. Gerda kisses Kai on the lips to warm him and free him from the lake. Gerda and Kai, then work together to finish Kai\u2019s task so they can leave her realm. When they spell the word eternity, the doorway out of the Snow Queen\u2019s castle opens and they begin the long journey back to town in Denmark. However, when they returned to their town</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">They meet Hans Christian Anderson, the Changeling Monarch of the Court of Ash and Snow. He informed them that the year was 1839, and over two hundred years had passed. He takes them back to the Freehold in Copenhagen to help them adjust to their new lives. He also wrote about their adventures in <i>First Volume of New Fairy Tales</i>.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This fairy tale has a happy ending in that Gerda and Kai were able to reform their strong bond of friendship. Sadly, Kai was never able to remove the glass from his eyes and the only good he can see is Gerda. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Note: </i>Both Gerda and Kai have the <b><i>Lost Boy </i></b>merit/flaw (They appear younger than twelve, but are over a hundred years old). Gerda is a fairest Truefriend, While Kai has his own unique kith, but no seeming since he was saved rather than saved himself.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T22:14:35-08:00","id":1059353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1059257#post1059257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't have to be a big list of wyrd 10 changes. The legendary Fae could be be examples of how to play variations of different types of immortals you can play. Like a lost boy, i.e. a changeling stuck in the form of a child, but have the minds of adults.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that sort of things just &quot;Changeling with appropriate kith + seeming combination&quot;. Things like that would be useful to see in a players guide though which goes through how seemings/kith can affect a changeling's mindset and experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T06:15:07-08:00","id":1059461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1059353#post1059353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that sort of things just &quot;Changeling with appropriate kith + seeming combination&quot;. Things like that would be useful to see in a players guide though which goes through how seemings/kith can affect a changeling's mindset and experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily, Wild Sam was a Playmate Fairest who had been stuck in child form by his durance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:00:57-08:00","id":1059650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1059461#post1059461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not necessarily, Wild Sam was a Playmate Fairest who had been stuck in child form by his durance.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by not necessarily? Achieving &quot;stuck in child form&quot; from Playmate Fairest is an example of &quot;Changeling with appropriate kith + seeming combination&quot; causing being stuck in child form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T15:12:58-08:00","id":1059776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1059650#post1059650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by not necessarily? Achieving &quot;stuck in child form&quot; from Playmate Fairest is an example of &quot;Changeling with appropriate kith + seeming combination&quot; causing being stuck in child form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither the first seeming nor the playmate kith stick you in child form. In Changeling 1e, Playmates gained +2 to any teamwork role where they are the primary actor and the fairest seeming allowed you to spend glamor to increase your dice pools in presence, persuasion, and manipulate rolls. Pus if you remember Winter Masks, it mentions that the fairest aged poorly compared to other seemings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T17:17:23-08:00","id":1059834,"title":"","content":"Here are some idea for Epic Changeling merits.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\"><i>Pure-Heart(3 dots)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>wyrd 7</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Effect: </b>The Player must decide if their character is an epic hero or villain. If the character is a hero, they completely refreshes his willpower pool when fulfilling his virtue and a villain completely refreshes his willpower when indulging his vice.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Drawback: </b>Trying to refill your dice pool through the opposite channel if greatly increased. Ignore two successes for your vice if a hero or your virtue if you are a villain. Also, such roles don\u2019t gain the benefits of the 10 again rule.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\"><i>Potent Seeming(3 dots)</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Prerequisite: </b>seeming, wyrd 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Effect: </b>By your actions and the power of your wyrd, you seeming begins to bleed into your mask and give your mien new abilities and qualities.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>examples:</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Beasts gain functioning characteristics of their animal(fur/pelt, scales, gills, prehensile tail, extra arms and legs) including characteristics of legendary monsters like the toxic skin of a Nuckelavee or the deadly gaze of a Basilisk. They may even gain powers associated with their animal like the nine lives of a cat or the hypnotic gaze of a serpent.</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Darklings gain the ability to see in the dark and other scenes that usually suffer a -1 to perception. They may also lose features that allow people to track them like fingerprints, foot prints, and scent. They may become fluid as a shadow.</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Elementals gain immunity to the effects of their element and even some of its features (bark skin, the fluidity of water, or being light enough to balance on a leaf). And their presence really CAN influence mortals.</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b><i>Drawback: </i></b>Their curse strengthens as well. Beasts might gain a derangement associated with their animal(cats an incredible fear or water, monkeys become unable to ignore their curiosity), Darklings with a high enough wyrd suffer aggravated damage from sunlight, ect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Note: I can see many players arguing that the function of this merit is met with potent seeming and dual kith. This merit makes sense to me, because your seeming represents how you took your life back, how you regained your right to make your own decisions. As such, along with access to in seeming contracts, I can see some changelings continuing to follow the path that allowed them to escape from their keepers gaining access to more powers/abilities from their seeming.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T17:26:27-08:00","id":1059836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1059776#post1059776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neither the first seeming nor the playmate kith stick you in child form.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason Playmate + Fairest couldn't leave you in child form. Each kith + seeming combination isn't limited to a single appearance, the ones in Chapter One are merely examples. As long as it makes sense you can have it as your appearance, and that makes perfect sense for that combination.<br /> <br /> Also, something makes me very amused by a Pure-Hearted changeling with a lazy vice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T17:42:00-08:00","id":1059845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1059836#post1059836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no reason Playmate + Fairest couldn't leave you in child form. Each kith + seeming combination isn't limited to a single appearance, the ones in Chapter One are merely examples. As long as it makes sense you can have it as your appearance, and that makes perfect sense for that combination.<br /> <br /> Also, something makes me very amused by a Pure-Hearted changeling with a lazy vice.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you still Age, which affects your mask and mien.<br /> <br /> Also , I would like to hear your ideas for a Pure-Hearted Changeling with the lazy vice<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T20:12:28-08:00","id":1059904,"title":"","content":"I could see an argument that high wyrd could force you into a child form by raw, it should be completely the optional, but personally I despise the idea of playing children, memories of childhood is not something I generally find pleasant or fun, but others have had different experiences in childhood, made different choices, and so maybe for others playing children brings back found memories, but it doesn't for me. <br /> <br /> But maybe that is more reason to play one some day if that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T20:31:02-08:00","id":1059911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1059904#post1059904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see an argument that high wyrd could force you into a child form by raw, it should be completely the optional, but personally I despise the idea of playing children, memories of childhood is not something I generally find pleasant or fun, but others have had different experiences in childhood, made different choices, and so maybe for others playing children brings back found memories, but it doesn't for me.<br /> <br /> But maybe that is more reason to play one some day if that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to find inspiration for playing a darker, grimmer version of an adult trapped in a child's body, I recommend the black comedy, I Hate Fairyland.<br /> <br /> Also, I was envisioning the concept of changeling's who had been taken as children and their experiences kept them from aging. When they return to Earth, they find that they have stopped aging.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T20:39:46-08:00","id":1059915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1059845#post1059845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you still Age, which affects your mask and mien.<br /> <br /> Also , I would like to hear your ideas for a Pure-Hearted Changeling with the lazy vice<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It would affect your mask, but not your mien.... maybe. Depends on your interpretation of how mien and mask interact. But your mien shouldn't change, your mien is the perfect childhood playmate so you should stay as that. And you can take the merit which pauses your aging's appearance/effects during character creation, or just have high enough wyrd + that merit which doubles your wyrd for the purposes of aging.<br /> <br /> As for the lazy villain. <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/OrcusOnHisThrone\" target=\"_blank\">Orcus on his Throne</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1059904#post1059904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see an argument that high wyrd could force you into a child form by raw, it should be completely the optional, but personally I despise the idea of playing children, memories of childhood is not something I generally find pleasant or fun, but others have had different experiences in childhood, made different choices, and so maybe for others playing children brings back found memories, but it doesn't for me.<br /> <br /> But maybe that is more reason to play one some day if that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot really see there being any RAW which force your mien to look like X if you take Y option. Seems very against the ridiculously dynamic rules for kiths and combining them with seemings. Though, I expect a &quot;Your forever a kid&quot; to be in the Personal Horror file rather than the Slice of Life Fun file for the same reason vampiric children are horrific in fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T20:42:17-08:00","id":1059916,"title":"","content":"The Changeling stuck in the form of a child (which I will call a Lost Boy) can be an NPC. Also, rather than using a character to emphasize the joys of childhood, I would use a character to emphasize the tragedy and grimness of such and existence. Think of having to live through middle school for decades. Such a character would have to travel constantly to keep people from questioning why they don't age. Plus, the people who were important to them in childhood might be gone (either died of old age or simply moved away and the Lost Boy can't find them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T21:25:40-08:00","id":1059924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1059904#post1059904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see an argument that high wyrd could force you into a child form by raw, .</div> </div> </div> </div>I envision a Changeling being trapped in the form of a child through the machinations of the True Fae rather than the power of the Wyrd. The Wyrd symbolizes transformation, development wile being stuck in the form of a child is stagnation.<br /> <br /> As for why the True Fae would do this... I can see a tone of reasons. It might be because the True Fae wants a childhood playmate. Maybe the True Fae wants to experience the joys of a parent nurturing a small child. Maybe the True Fae wants to understand innocence or how to corrupt it. Maybe the role the changeling plays is that of the child or children who goes on a magical adventure where they enter a fairy tale land make friends while defeating enemies before returning home (The Wizard of Oz, Chronicles of Narnia, Peter Pan, Alice in Wonderland).<br /> <br /> Rather than being part of a kith, I see it as a merit/flaw(which I will call <b><i>Lost Boy</i></b>) that is complemented with a kith like DearHeart, Playmate, TrueFriend, ect.<br /> <br /> I see this being done to changelings who had been stolen as children, but if the True Fae is a Genie/Djinn, Wish Master type Fae, they may do it as a twist on a wish a mortal makes. Example, 98 year old man wishes to be made young immortal, and never aging.. POOF! The True Fae turns him into a six year old child.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T22:16:56-08:00","id":1060418,"title":"","content":"I am actually pretty fond of my Potent Seeming merit, so I want to defend against the idea that the potent kith, dual kith merits and seeming contracts fulfill the mechanics and surrounding the Potent Seeming idea.<br /> <br /> A changeling can develop potent kith or dual kith the way a person develops a skill or muscle; through training, practice, and exercise.<br /> <br /> To develop Potent Seeming, however, a Changeling has to continue to play the role that allowed them to escape from Arcadia; A Fairest continues to be a hero, protecting changelings from the Hunstmen that stalk them, foiling the plans of loyalists and soulless in freeholds, even starting social movements.<br /> <br /> Darkling continue to be people who work in the shadows both literally and figuratively, developing their skills in larceny, stealth, and subterfuge to survive, moving only during times of darkness, and isolating themselves from much of changeling society.<br /> <br /> Rather continuing to be animals that hunt and survive in the wilds, Beasts emphasize the qualities associated with specific animals; being as proud as a lion, cold hearted and treacherous as a snake (lawyers and investment bankers), being as curious as monkey, or a stubborn as a goat. Becoming the animal characters we see in folk tales and fairy tales.<br /> <br /> As for seeming contracts fulfilling the mechanics in this concept... while buying contracts of a seeming does give you some of their features associated with the seeming even if you are not a part of it, my understanding is that they are cosmetic and don't give you the benefits of having fur, gills, bark skin, ect. Potent seeming makes these features functional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T17:22:43-08:00","id":1060703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1059916#post1059916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Changeling stuck in the form of a child (which I will call a Lost Boy) can be an NPC. Also, rather than using a character to emphasize the joys of childhood, I would use a character to emphasize the tragedy and grimness of such and existence. Think of having to live through middle school for decades. Such a character would have to travel constantly to keep people from questioning why they don't age. Plus, the people who were important to them in childhood might be gone (either died of old age or simply moved away and the Lost Boy can't find them)</div> </div> </div> </div>I can also see <i>Lost Boys</i> creepy antagonists. Drawing on the themes of Lord of the Flies and Children of the Corn, the Lost boys might be loyalists who worship their keeper as a god. They sacrifice adults to it and kidnap human children to be turned into Lost Boys like them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T20:22:48-08:00","id":1061423,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><i>Alice Liddell: </i></b>Along time ago, or to be more specific, in a rowing boat on The Isis/River Thames July 4, 1862, young Alice Pleasance Liddell told Charles Lutwig Dodgson( who would write under the pseudonym Lewsis Caroll) a most peculiar story. She described how she followed a white rabbit down a rabbit hole and found herself in the magical world of Wonderland. While there, she befriended a Mad Hatter, March Hare, the twins Tweedledum and Tweedledee, the Cheshire Cat, as well as the White Rabbit, himself. She rescues them from the foul tempered and murderous Queen of Hearts, escapes from the Harpy Bird, Bandersnatch, and even slays her most terrifying monster, the Jabberwocky. Charles Ludwig is so intrigued by her story that he writes down an edited version titled, <i>Alice in Wonderland.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sadly, in June of 1863, relationships between Charles Lutwig Dodgson a.k.a Lewis Caroll, and the Liddells meets with a sudden break. Some speculate that this is because Charles Lutwig wanted to marry little Alice, but whatever the reasons the Liddells forbid Charles from seeing her. Heartbroken, Charles Lutwig tried to move on with his life. However, much to his great shock, he met Alice again in 1869. She told him a tale of how she went <i>Through the Looking Glass </i>and came to a chess world ruled between a White Queen and a Red Queen. Both led two factions that fought for dominance. Lewis Caroll once again wrote about the world she detailed and the book was published in 1871.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Lewis Caroll died worshipping his Alice, his muse, his queen, his goddess. The Alice Liddell that married, became Alice Hargreaves, and died at the age of 82 was Alice\u2019s fetch. Alice Liddell, herself, does not look at day past the age of ten, but is an extremely powerful wyrd 10 changeling. She leads an entitlement of the Courts of Ash and Snow that is connected to the tales of Alice in Wonderland and Through the Looking Glass. It\u2019s members include the White Rabbit, the Mad Hatter, the March Hare, Tweedledum and Tweedledee, the Cheshire Cat, and even Humpty Dumpty.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Alice Liddell is a Lost Girl of the Fairest seeming. Rather than being a Playmate, Truefriend, or Dearheart, I wanted to give her a seeming that is connected to madness, the innocence of a child, or dreams. This is how I envision her blessing, the storyteller can giver her visions that giver her insight into the stories main plot line, her madness/innocence protects her from mind altering supernatural powers. Because she has potent kith, her blessing allows her to warp reality (connected to the idea of madness or childhood fantasy, if she believes she can fly, she can fly, if she think a piece of cake will cause her to grow to the size of a giant, it will do so), she can also use a version of the madness network that allows her to see through the eyes of children or the insane. </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T15:29:21-07:00","id":1064056,"title":"","content":"An interesting wyrd 10 Changeling storyline to explore would be one that focused on the story of <b><i>Journey to the West. </i></b>The story is based on an actual event, the pilgrimage of a Tang dynasty Buddhist monk, Xuanzang, to India so an East Asian Changeling chronicle could be used to explore the historical and mythical history of this work. Plus, I would LOVE to see Son Wukung, the Monkey King and inspiration for heroes like Son Goku as a wyrd 10 changeling<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I could easily see him as a wyrd 10 changeling with dual kith, the potent seeming merit for both kiths, plus my idea of potent seeming<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T15:47:49-07:00","id":1066607,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I remember on this thread, the description of what a draconic darkling would look like. This churned in my head as I was thinking of mythical heroes and villains to be transformed into wyrd 10 changelings. I am surprised it took me this long, but I eventually realized, the Arthurian arch villain Mordred, would be the perfect folk villain to be reinvisioned as a darkling draconic. Thank\u2019s to Sir Thomas Mallory\u2019s popular interpretation of the Arthurian cycle, most of us know/envision Mordred as the traitorous son of King Arthur. However, Mordred\u2019s beginnings are more diverse than that.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mordred is first mentioned in Annales Cambriae, in the year 539. In this version, his name is Medraut, and a rival of King Arthur rather than a traitorous follower. Geoffrey of Monmouth developed the more familiar image of Mordred as Arthur\u2019s traitorous nephew and the son of Lancelot. It is sir Thomas Malory\u2019s Arthurian cycle that developed the popular version of Mordred as King Arthur\u2019s traitorous son.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If Mordred were introduced as a changeling in Changeling the Lost, I would actually like to explore the earliest versions of the tale of him being a rival rather than a traitor. Partly this is because I want to explore how myths and legends change over time and how rumor can totally distort a person\u2019s real character.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T19:29:43-07:00","id":1067318,"title":"","content":"In the discussions of whether or not to use popular fairytale folk heroes/villains in a rule book that focuses on epic/legendary/wyrd 10 changelings, one developer stated that they would rather focus on the least well known legends. My argument for using the characters of popular tales is that you can explore the dark origins or darker versions of the myths.<br /> <br /> Case in point, Aladdin. Contrary to the popular Disney version of Aladdin as a heroic and noble figure, the original Alladin was impetuous, lazy, and stupid. His father dies of disappointment in the beginning of the story. To prove his worth, he is determined to marry the princess.....who happens to already be betrothed. In order to annul the marriage, Aladdin kidnaps the princess, sleeps with her, and has his djinn torture her fianc\u00e9. When a sorcerer banishes Aladdin's kingdom out of revenge for steal the djinn lamp, Alladin has the princess (who just happens to be Alladin's wife) seduce, sleep with the sorcerer, the cut his throat.<br /> <br /> There is also a Chinese version of Aladdin, where after he escapes from the cave of wonders, he goes on a murderous rampage trying to find the sorcerer... and that's where they story ends<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T21:03:25-07:00","id":1067371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1067318#post1067318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the discussions of whether or not to use popular fairytale folk heroes/villains in a rule book that focuses on epic/legendary/wyrd 10 changelings, one developer stated that they would rather focus on the least well known legends. My argument for using the characters of popular tales is that you can explore the dark origins or darker versions of the myths.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just weird if changelings are the origins of fairytales, being humans changed by fairytale logic and altered to follow tropes requires the fairytales and tropes to exist beforehand or they would end up being changed into something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 03-24-2017, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T21:54:41-07:00","id":1067396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1067371#post1067371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just weird if changelings are the origins of fairytales, being humans changed by fairytale logic and altered to follow tropes requires the fairytales and tropes to exist beforehand or they would end up being changed into something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think an epic changeling book should imply (or at least allow to be explored) the idea that True Fae were, if not created, given form by human myths. You also have to remember that before there were fairy tales, there were mythologies and legends about Pagan gods. An epic Changeling book can suggest that such legends were what allowed the True Fae to first enter the mortal/human realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T01:34:07-07:00","id":1067453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1067396#post1067396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also have to remember that before there were fairy tales, there were mythologies and legends about Pagan gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes that's part of my point. Your &quot;snow white&quot; wouldn't be made be to be like snow-white by the wyrd, her form would be based on tropes from mythologies making her drastically different (especially since mythology and folklore operate on completely different styles of tropes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:37:33-07:00","id":1067579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1067453#post1067453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes that's part of my point. Your &quot;snow white&quot; wouldn't be made be to be like snow-white by the wyrd, her form would be based on tropes from mythologies making her drastically different (especially since mythology and folklore operate on completely different styles of tropes).</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to remember that the major for theme of Changeling the lost is taking back your identity and making the story your own. I don't see there being multiple versions of a fairytales causing forcing a changeling's mien to constantly change, because the fairy tale was how you took your life back. I can actually see a wyrd 10 changeling gaining power from it though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:15:17-07:00","id":1067662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1067396#post1067396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think an epic changeling book should imply (or at least allow to be explored) the idea that True Fae were, if not created, given form by human myths. You also have to remember that before there were fairy tales, there were mythologies and legends about Pagan gods. An epic Changeling book can suggest that such legends were what allowed the True Fae to first enter the mortal/human realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me further explain this. One idea I have for the origins of the True Fae draws inspiration from the Fair Folk/Raksha from the Exalted Universe. That is.. that the True Fae were originally shapeless entities trapped outside of the mortal realm. As humans began to worship and develop myths about their gods, the True Fae discovered that they could enter the mortal realm and gain identity and shape by tapping into and harvesting these myths. They also developed their realms in Arcadia by drawing on human myths.<br /> <br /> The flip side was that Changelings discovered that they could develop their own myths to defeat the True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T14:52:59-07:00","id":1067800,"title":"","content":"A fairy tale that I think would work really well in a <i><b>Changeling: The Lost</b></i> setting, is the story of <i>Undine.</i> The story begins with a fisherman's daughter drowning, when she falls into a lake. However, the next morning, they find her wet and asleep in her cot (some versions imply while others state outright that undine was exchanged for a nymphs daughter and is a changeling). The child is very quit and mild. However, when they take her to a church to be baptized and prayers are said, the child begins to shriek and throw and tantrum. As Undine grows up, she become an extremely beautiful woman, but due to not having a soul, she is also very selfish. One day, a knight comes to the fisherman's cottage and upon seeing Undine, falls in love with her. After strong hesitation from Undine's father, the fisherman, the knight eventually convinces him to allow the knight to marry Undine. While the knight and Undine are traveling back to his kingdom, he makes a vow to love her for all of eternity. During the marriage, God gives Undine a soul, which makes her sweet and gentle. In the knight's kingdom, it just so happens that they knight has a lady friend who is also in love with him. Initially, she and Undine get along well, but once she learns that Undine is a water spirit, she sets all her power of persuasion to convince the knight that Undine is a malevolent spirit.<br /> <br /> Tragically, the girl's poisoned words begin to take hold and Undine is pained to see the knight's love for her leave his eyes. One day, Undine, the knight, and the girl are horse riding, when the girl loses her necklace. The knight and his girlfriend accuse Undine of dropping the necklace in the river. When Undine reaches her hand in and brings up a more beautiful necklace, the knight cries, &quot;you are no Maiden! you are an evil witch! Away! return to the lake and bother us no more!&quot; In despair, Undine throws herself into the water, never to be seen again. The Knight and his girlfriend plan on getting married. However, on the night of their wedding a watery figure that looks a lot like Undine pulls herself out of the well and states &quot;You promised to love me for all eternity, now you must pay with your life.&quot; and the knight dies.<br /> <br /> \u200bI can hear a lot of people saying &quot;That's not How the story goes!&quot; My defense is that there are variations of this tale and this is the one I enjoy most.<br /> <br /> If I were to introduce Undine in a Changeling chronicle, I would make her a waterborne elemental, winter courtier, and duchess of the ice bound heart.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T16:37:59-07:00","id":1067839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1067579#post1067579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need to remember that the major for theme of Changeling the lost is taking back your identity and making the story your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on that changelings would have their kiths altered by their seemings and they'd all get to just choose their appearance.... The wyrd alters how changelings look to follow storytropes, and the only way to change that is by going back and escaping in a different way. The wyrd isn't going to change you into a story that doesn't exist yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see there being multiple versions of a fairytales causing forcing a changeling's mien to constantly change, because the fairy tale was how you took your life back. </div> </div> </div>What? What does this have anything to do with the conversation?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T16:59:16-07:00","id":1067848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1067839#post1067839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on that changelings would have their kiths altered by their seemings and they'd all get to just choose their appearance.... The wyrd alters how changelings look to follow storytropes, and the only way to change that is by going back and escaping in a different way. The wyrd isn't going to change you into a story that doesn't exist yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't talking about their appearance changing, rather that when escaping, the Changeling takes the story the True Fae set for them and made it there own. The second part of my argument was that there being multiple versions of a fairy tale did not mean that a Changeling's mien is constantly changing. My impression is that True Fae and Changelings (those of wyrd 10, at least) can gain a certain degree of power as legends and folktales surrounding them become more popular and well known.<br /> <br /> My earlier point of there being myths and legends older than our more popular fairytales was to emphasize that just because the True Fae were the first to use the myths to gain influence to the mortal world does not exclude Changelings from learning to do the same. Just as changelings learning to use contracts, I think they can also use fairy tales to increase their power and drive the True Fae's influence from the mortal realm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T19:40:00-07:00","id":1067891,"title":"","content":"It feels like your just having a conversation on your own and not understanding my points so I'm just going to leave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T20:01:37-07:00","id":1067895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1067371#post1067371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just weird if changelings are the origins of fairytales, being humans changed by fairytale logic and altered to follow tropes requires the fairytales and tropes to exist beforehand or they would end up being changed into something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the best way to explain my view of True Fae and Changeling's connection to mythologies and fairytales is based on how I separate True Fae from Changelings. As my thread on True Fae inspirations emphasize, I envision True Fae as the pagan gods and Leviathans, and Emperors of Hell that humans worshipped. Changelings are the fairytale heroes, villains(wyrd 1 through 6), demigods, spirits, greater faerie monsters, prince and princesses of hell(wyrd 7 to 9) that opposed or supported the True Fae. The True Fae are connected to the myths of the Asgardians, Jotuns, Firbolgs, Formorians, Olympians, Titans while changelings are connected to faerie tales of prince and princesses, evil witches, giants, trolls, and man eating wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T13:07:58-07:00","id":1068076,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><i>Hansel and Gretel\u2019s</i></b> story begins just before the Black Death burst on the world stage, in the year 1316. After the European economy imploded and the little Ice Age of 1300 had begun. When people were so desperate that they were digging up graves to eat the corpses of the dead\u2026.. and they began eating each other. In a part of Europe that would become Germany a husband and wife were talking to each other. They did not have enough food to feed themselves and certainly not their son and daughter, Hansel and Gretel. The wife told the husband to take the children to the woods and leave them there. When they were abandoned and knowing that their parents would would kill and eat them if they returned, they decided to seek survival in the forest. After walking a distance, they were astonished to come upon a house made of gingerbread, cakes, and candy. Starving, they fell upon the house like ravenous wolves. What they did not know was that the house was a lure for a True Fae in the form of a man eating hag. The had quickly snatches Hansel and Gretel, spiriting them away to her realm in Arcadia. There, she fattens Hansel up by forcing him to eat the the flesh of changelings escaping their keeper\u2019s realms, humans, and hobgoblins. The Hag makes Gretel her slave, but also teaches her the secrets of witchcraft for some reason.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Hag has a minor bane, which she carries with her in her realm in Arcadia. She is blind</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">, which the children use to her advantage, using a bone to convince the terrifying Crone the Hasel in thin, when he has actually become monstrously fat. Her second major weakness is connected to her True Fae nature, she lacks creativity. After growing frustrated that Hansel is not fattening up, she decides to eat both of them. Gretel pretends not to understand when the witch asks her to check the stove. Infuriated, the Hag demonstrates and Gretel pushes her in and shuts the stoves door. This is the major bane of the True Fae and while it does not kill the True Fae, it DOES destroy that actor and removes a great deal of its power. This allows Hansel and Gretel to escape her realm and eventually return to medieval Europe.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">When they return to the mortal realm, they join the Autumn Court and build dual identities as witch and witch hunter. In their lives as changelings, they participate in all of the Autumn courts heathen rituals and spreading fear as well as developing their powers over the occult. In their mortal lives, they were fanatical participants in the witch hunts of Germany, personally taking part in the arrests, torture and burning of accused witches throughout the 14 through 1600s. Presently, these grotesques serve as the German Autumn Court\u2019s most frightening inquisitors.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Hansel is a ogre seeming Gristlegrinder with five dots in the potent kith merit. He can do bite attacks without needing to grapple and bite deals +10 lethal damage. He is also capable of digesting non-edible foods like bike tires, car parts, silver utensil, ect. He is also immune to bashing and lethal damagee, though he take aggravated damage normally. Finally, his fat acts a form of armor that protects him not only from edged weapons and fire arms, but also falling debris, missiles, hot and cold effects. He can also hold/hide items in the folds of his fat. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Gretel is a darkling of the Witchtooth kith. She has the potent kith merit, which gives her the 9, 8, and 7 again rule in all occult roles. Her blessing also has the effects of the five levels of the defunct Vampire: The Masquerade discipline Maleficia, the Dark Thaumaturgy Path of Pain, and access to the scrying merit, which she activates with glamor. Her sense of smell is so keen, she can not only smell where people are, but what they are feeling.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T07:25:09-07:00","id":1072516,"title":"","content":"I fully support giving more attention to the less known myths and fables.<br /> <br /> Also, why not go beyond just listing Kiths, Seemings and powers? I think we can do better. How about we focus on how the tales of these characters change over time? Some of these characters might still be alive (or have heirs/disciples/descendants). They probably have a thing or two to say about the stories we have been telling about them. In other cases, changelings of today might take on their classic roles, but with modern sensibilities, often becoming Grimms and/or joining appropriate Courts. What happens when these two meet each other? Can the old and new tales co-exist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-03-2017, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T15:44:47-07:00","id":1072738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1072516#post1072516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fully support giving more attention to the less known myths and fables.<br /> <br /> Also, why not go beyond just listing Kiths, Seemings and powers? I think we can do better. How about we focus on how the tales of these characters change over time? Some of these characters might still be alive (or have heirs/disciples/descendants). They probably have a thing or two to say about the stories we have been telling about them. In other cases, changelings of today might take on their classic roles, but with modern sensibilities, often becoming Grimms and/or joining appropriate Courts. What happens when these two meet each other? Can the old and new tales co-exist?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be fascinating to have a changeling scenario where the original legend meets the changelings who are copying him<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I also hope they explore the historical reality behind the fairytales like the real Robin hood being a wellborn cut throat and the Pied Piper of Hamlin being a pedophile psychopath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T19:46:21-07:00","id":1082493,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Pinnocchio</b></i><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Along time ago, in the mid1800\u2019s there was an elderly impoverished, woodcarver named Geppetto. Geppetto had a son, who was a rascal, imp, rogue, disgrace, and even Geppetto referred to him as \u201ca wretched boy.\u201d His son\u2019s name was Pinnocchio. One day, a talking crickets, (who has lived in Geppetto\u2019s house for over a hundred years) warns Pinnocchio of the dangers of disobedience and hedonism. Pinnocchio thanks the cricket by killing it with a hammer. Thus, does Pinnocchio\u2019s misfortune begin.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">On his way to school, Pinnocchio see\u2019s a puppet theater is being put on. Deciding to sell his school book (which Geppetto sacrificed his only woolen jacket to buy), Pinnocchio obtains a ticket eager to see the show. Much to his horror, however, <i>the Great Puppet Master Mangiafuoco, </i>carves him into wood a ties him up with strings. Pinnochio becomes one of <i>Mangiafuoco\u2019s</i> marionettes\u2019 putting on performances for the Gentry. In his place, <i>Mangiafuoco</i> creates a boy of thread, wool, and hay, with five gold coins for Geppetto.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Day after day, night after night, Pinnocchio is forced to sing and dance for the True Fae, putting on the most painful, humiliating and entertaining acts for the True Fae. However, the Gentry find Pinnocchio duller and duller and he fears that <i>Mangiafuoco </i>will chop in into firewood. While <i>Mangiafuoco</i> is counting his money, Pinnocchio manages to escape. While fleeing into the Hedge, he comes across a freehold buried deep in the brambles. Stopping for a draft of beer, he meets a Fox and Cat, who after drinking and wenching with them, abandon him to pay for their meal. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">While traveling through the Hedge, he is ambushed by the Fox and Cat, who are actually racketeers, planning to sell Pinocchio to the highest bidder among the True Fae. Entertaining themselves, by hanging him from a tree and watching him swing. When they leave him, he is rescued by a motley of a Fairst(the Blue Fairy), a Falcon, and a Poodle. They take him to their freehold, where Pinnocchio must work for food. Tired of working, begin\u2019s his quest to return to Geppetto\u2019s cottage.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Along the way, Pinnochio meet\u2019s the <i>Coachman,</i> who has a coach full of children. <i>The Coachman</i> promises to take Pinnocchio to Toyland, a place where children do nothing but play all day. On the Fifth day, however, Pinnocchio and all the children have turned into donkeys and are sold to a circus where they are forced to perform tricks. However, Pinnocchio sprains his leg, and is skinned and thrown into the ocean.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Once again a puppet, Pinnocchio swims through the Ocean, but is swallowed by a <i>Dogfish</i> larger than an island. For an entire year, Pinnocchio lives inside the <i>Dogfish</i>, eating the water the beast swallows. One day, however, Pinnocchio gathers enough wood to start a fire, which suffocates the <i>Dogfish</i> and forces it to the surface.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Escaping, he returns to the brambles of the Hedge and finally finds a doorway back to the mortal world. At the entrance, he meets the Cat and Fox, who have been tortured and maimed for letting Pinnocchio escape. Pinnocchio mocked them and stated that their misfortune served them right for their wickedness.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Pinnocchio finally came to Geppetto\u2019s cottage convinced that he would be able to regain the life he lost. However, there was another boy there who Geppetto loved even greater than he. For this boy was a dutiful son, who took care of Geppetto in his ailing health, studied hard at school, and even works at a farm to help support Geppetto.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Unable to regain his old life, Pinnochio steals the identity of Carlo Collodi, an Italian children\u2019s writer, and writes a HIGHLY edited version of his misadventures in Arcadia and the Hedge. </span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T17:09:22-07:00","id":1083229,"title":"","content":"In my discussions about doing an Epic Changeling rulebook, I have emphasized my interest in exploring the dark origins/realities behind some of our favorite fairy tales (<i>\u200bNote: I do hope that a scorebook is done, exploring some of the least well known and creepy fairy tales from around the world. I just think they should be done in an international Changeling book).</i> One of of our favorite folk heroes I is explored is Robin Hood, who was a wellborn cutthroat rather than a heroic figure who gave to the poor. <br /> <br /> One of the ways I hope Onyx Path explores the true story of Robin Hood is by looking at his relationship with the Sheriff of Nottingham, one of the most libeled law enforcement officers in history. Not that I think the Sheriff of Nottingham should be made a tragically heroic figure. I see him as a figure of his time, someone who was both bully and bullied; intimidating and ruthless toward the English peasantry, but a brutalized victim of the English nobility and than the True Fae.<br /> <br /> I see him as the perfect character for a wyrd 10 Ogre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T21:57:41-07:00","id":1085362,"title":"","content":"I found an old legend that, although focusing on a ghost like character, could easily be reinterpreted as a Changeling. I also think he would make an interesting word 10 changeling though I can see people stating he would make a better huntsman.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Herne the Hunter</i></b> <span style=\"color:#171717\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u2018Herne\u2019 </i>was one of the keepers of the \u2018<i>Forest of Windsor\u2019</i> in the reign of \u2018<i>King Richard II\u2019</i> and known for his great hunting and woodcraft skills. Whilst King Richard favoured Herne his fellow hunters it is said hated him and plotted to cause Herne\u2019s downfall.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#171717\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One day the royal party were out on a hunt the king was nearly killed when attacked by a stag. Herne stepped in to help the king taking the main blow and fell to the floor. He seemed to be dead. Suddenly a dark figure appeared amongst the party and announced himself as \u2018<i>Philip Urswick\u2019</i>. He then proceeded to inform the king that for a reward he would cure Herne.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#171717\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">After cutting the head off the stag and binding it to Herne\u2019s head, the party took Herne to Urswick\u2019s own hut which was located on \u2018<i>Bagshot Heath\u2019</i>. Urswick vowed that he would take great care of Herne. King Richard then announced that if Herne recovered he would promote Herne to be the chief keeper.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#171717\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unbeknown to the king the other hunters were later in contact with Urswick and told him of their loathing for the favoured keeper announcing that they were disappointed that he had not died in the incident. Urswick promised the hunters revenge but only if his first wish and the reward was granted. He told them that Herne would recover but would loose all his hunting skills. Satisfied with his answer, the hunters agreed.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#171717\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keeping his promise to the king it seemed, Urswick soon had Herne returned to court whereupon he was promoted to chief keeper. Herne seemed to have recovered thoroughly until it became apparent that his hunting skills had disappeared. The king was extremely disappointed with Herne revoked the promotion. It is said that this is the reason why Herne, being so grieved by the king\u2019s actions, hanged himself from an Oak tree in Windsor forest. His body disappeared under suspicious circumstances.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#171717\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Urswick did not reveal the charm that he had cast upon Herne to the king. A new chief hunter was appointed but he too, once promoted, lost his skill. The same happened to his successor too. Urswick was asked to remove the charm. Before making any agreement, Urswick informed the hunters that they would have to meet him at the Oak. Once there they would be told what had to be done to dispel the charm.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#171717\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The group of hunters arrived at the Oak as asked and after waiting a short time Urswick appeared. He told the them that Herne\u2019s death was on each of them and that horses and hounds should be brought to the oak the next night. Agreeing they made preparations and returned to the forest. On reaching the Oak Herne appeared on a horse and told them to follow him to another area of the forest. Herne took the party to a Beech tree and whilst there Urswick suddenly appeared out of the tree covered in flames. Herne had summoned Urswick to appear. Urswick then made the party swear an oath to Herne that they would form a band of hunters with Herne as their leader to dispel the charm.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#171717\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Urswick\u2019s promise had been satisfied and the hunters became a faithful if not loving band of men loyal to Herne. For many nights the group would raid the forest taking deer until very few were left. King Richard came to learn of their pursuits, and decided to make a visit to he oak. He was angry and desired revenge upon the men.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#171717\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once there Herne appeared to the king and learnt of his anger. Herne listened and said that if the king wished him to leave the forest, taking his power with him, the king would have to agree to a request. Doubtless Herne wanted revenge upon his enemies who had desired his death. The king agreed to his request, and the group of men were hanged. Herne was then never seen again.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#171717\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is reputed though that Herne returned and reigned supreme, taking control of the forest of Windsor for eight years after the death of King Richard.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#171717\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Many versions of the Herne legend exist. Some say that Herne hanged himself after committing a terrible crime, whilst another tells of a forest demon that takes on his appearance. The demon is said to place stag horns on its head haunting the forest still trying to convince keepers that it is Herne and that they should sell their souls to him.</span></span> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#171717\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><i><u>\u2018The Merry Wives of Windsor\u2019 : William Shakespeare</u></i></b></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#171717\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><i>\u2018There is an old tale goes, that Herne the hunter,</i><br /> <i>Sometime a keeper here in Windsor forest,</i><br /> <i>Doth all the winter time at still midnight,</i><br /> <i>Walk around about an oak, with great ragg\u2019d horns;</i><br /> <i>And there he blasts the tree, and takes the cattle;</i><br /> <i>And makes milch-kine yield blood, and shakes a chain</i><br /> <i>In a most hideous and dreadful manner.\u2019</i></b></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#171717\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><i><u>The Merry Wives of Windsor : William Shakespeare</u></i></b></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#171717\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b><i>\u2018Why, yet there want not many, that do fear</i><br /> <i>In deep of night to walk by this Herne\u2019s oak.\u2019</i></b></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#171717\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">On <i>August 31 1863</i> the famous Windsor Oak fell from natural causes, but was soon replaced by a new young Oak tree by <i>Queen Victoria</i> on the same spot.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T13:17:56-07:00","id":1085554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1072516#post1072516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fully support giving more attention to the less known myths and fables.<br /> <br /> Also, why not go beyond just listing Kiths, Seemings and powers? I think we can do better. How about we focus on how the tales of these characters change over time? Some of these characters might still be alive (or have heirs/disciples/descendants). They probably have a thing or two to say about the stories we have been telling about them. In other cases, changelings of today might take on their classic roles, but with modern sensibilities, often becoming Grimms and/or joining appropriate Courts. What happens when these two meet each other? Can the old and new tales co-exist?</div> </div> </div> </div>As wyrd 10 changelings can potentially live forever, I can see several of them still being alive, including King Arthur, Merlin,Robin Heud, Snow White, plus Hansel and Gretel.<br /> <br /> Along with seeing what these legendary Changelings might have to say about their legends , I think the ideal meeting the reality. I can see their being an entitlement representing the vision of Robin Hood and his Merry Men being ideal heroes, when they were nothing more than cut throats (Yeah, I know. I am beating this into the ground<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). In my head, I envision word 10 Changeling Robin Heud having a character similar to the Nosferatu Antediluvian, Absimiliard. What would happen if modern changelings from the Merrymen entitlement met the monstrous reality?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T20:00:28-07:00","id":1085663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1072738#post1072738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be fascinating to have a changeling scenario where the original legend meets the changelings who are copying him<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I also hope they explore the historical reality behind the fairytales like the real Robin hood being a wellborn cut throat and the Pied Piper of Hamlin being a pedophile psychopath.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd like to just comment here that the &quot;historical reality&quot; behind Robin Hood and the Pied Piper is anything but settled, and Manchester (author of &quot;A World Lit Only By Fire&quot;) is at best a mediocre scholar and appears to have pretty much made that whole &quot;The Pied Piper was a pedophile psychopath&quot; thing up, whole cloth. The fact is, we don't know who Robin Hood was, or if a &quot;Robin Hood&quot;character ever actually existed. Likewise, the disappearance of the &quot;children of Hameln&quot; is very much a mystery, and may not have involved literal children, rats, or a piper at all. Don't believe me? How about the Straight Dope?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.straightdope.com/columns/read/2060/was-the-pied-piper-of-hamelin-a-child-molester\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cst.brightspotcdn.com/de/a8/81b9a8fd47e483faf699814a0972/straight-dope-logo.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.straightdope.com/columns/read/2060/was-the-pied-piper-of-hamelin-a-child-molester\" target=\"_blank\"> Was the Pied Piper of Hamelin a child molester? </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.straightdope.com/columns/read/2060/was-the-pied-piper-of-hamelin-a-child-molester\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.straightdope.com/columns/read/2060/was-the-pied-piper-of-hamelin-a-child-molester </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A STAFF REPORT FROM THE STRAIGHT DOPE SCIENCE ADVISORY BOARD </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> Now, if you'd like to go those routes for the purposes of a game you're running, fine and dandy, but please don't go telling folks that we know the &quot;truth&quot; of things like this. I'm a multi-class Archaeologist/Historian in real life, and people spreading alternative historical facts around just gets up my nose.<br /> <br /> Okay, I'm done, on with the conversation.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11313-thunderwheel","name":"Thunderwheel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T20:41:05-07:00","id":1085669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thunderwheel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1085663#post1085663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd like to just comment here that the &quot;historical reality&quot; behind Robin Hood and the Pied Piper is anything but settled, and Manchester (author of &quot;A World Lit Only By Fire&quot;) is at best a mediocre scholar and appears to have pretty much made that whole &quot;The Pied Piper was a pedophile psychopath&quot; thing up, whole cloth. The fact is, we don't know who Robin Hood was, or if a &quot;Robin Hood&quot;character ever actually existed. Likewise, the disappearance of the &quot;children of Hameln&quot; is very much a mystery, and may not have involved literal children, rats, or a piper at all. Don't believe me? How about the Straight Dope?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.straightdope.com/columns/read/2060/was-the-pied-piper-of-hamelin-a-child-molester\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cst.brightspotcdn.com/de/a8/81b9a8fd47e483faf699814a0972/straight-dope-logo.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.straightdope.com/columns/read/2060/was-the-pied-piper-of-hamelin-a-child-molester\" target=\"_blank\"> Was the Pied Piper of Hamelin a child molester? </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.straightdope.com/columns/read/2060/was-the-pied-piper-of-hamelin-a-child-molester\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.straightdope.com/columns/read/2060/was-the-pied-piper-of-hamelin-a-child-molester </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A STAFF REPORT FROM THE STRAIGHT DOPE SCIENCE ADVISORY BOARD </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Now, if you'd like to go those routes for the purposes of a game you're running, fine and dandy, but please don't go telling folks that we know the &quot;truth&quot; of things like this. I'm a multi-class Archaeologist/Historian in real life, and people spreading alternative historical facts around just gets up my nose.<br /> <br /> Okay, I'm done, on with the conversation.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is unfair to call someone a mediocre scholar, because their view does not match your own. scholarly research is full of historians contracting each others views (whether the black death was really bubonic plague, whether Shakespeare existed, or what led to the events of the Salem witch trials are just some examples). Also you just state one source to vindicate your position.<br /> <br /> I am interested in learning more about your research and background on this subject. However you will need to give more background before I am convinced of your position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T21:51:54-07:00","id":1085689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1085669#post1085669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it is unfair to call someone a mediocre scholar, because their view does not match your own. scholarly research is full of historians contracting each others views (whether the black death was really bubonic plague, whether Shakespeare existed, or what led to the events of the Salem witch trials are just some examples). Also you just state one source to vindicate your position.<br /> <br /> I am interested in learning more about your research and background on this subject. However you will need to give more background before I am convinced of your position.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am a professional researcher and scholar. I take information from disparate sources, including archaeological work and written documents, and interpret them to create a cohesive story that helps to contextualize the past. I frequently use speculation to fill in gaps in the historical record, and when I do, I explicitly say so. And when I say something based on someone else's work, I cite it, so that other people can go to the source, verify, and make a judgement as to whether my interpretations are valid.<br /> <br /> I am not a German historian, but that's irrelevant because I don't have to be. Scholarship isn't just making stuff up; citing sources is a basic tenet of good scholarship. A little bit of quick internet research on the &quot;real&quot; story of the Pied Piper yields lots of results. Look at some of them, and pay special attention to the ones that give sources, like this one:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.medievalists.net/2014/12/pied-piper-hamelin-medieval-mass-abduction/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.medievalists.net/2014/12/...ass-abduction/</a><br /> <br /> There's a theme here. These people say that it isn't clear what the historical event that spawned the Piper story was, and they don't know because the sources are unclear (but none cited ever mention children's bodies). You called me out for &quot;only citing one source,&quot; but that source cited several, and Manchester didn't cite one at all. That makes his version unreliable. Note that that's not the same as 'false.' But if he doesn't cite a source, and lots of other folks cite sources that don't support his story....well then.<br /> <br /> It is completely fair to call Manchester a mediocre scholar. It's even fair to call him a poor one, because HE MAKES UN-SOURCED STATEMENTS AND PRESENTS THEM AS FACT. Other actual scholars of the region and period have commented on his shortcomings, reviews are available to the searcher. So you see, I'm not calling him mediocre because I disagree with him. I'm calling him mediocre because he's mediocre, and I presented an argument backed by evidence. Up to the reader to judge if it's valid, but do me the courtesy of not disagreeing with me just because you don't like what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> This will be the last time I post on the subject, because I have nothing further to add to my stance on the issue and this is a sideline from the topic. But since you called me out on my background before you'd consider my position, ask yourself this:<br /> <br /> Why are you so convinced Manchester is correct? Have you done research that supports his theory? If so, by all means, publish it, it would be a significant contribution to German historical scholarship. If not, then if you you want to know the &quot;truth&quot; about these things, start with the sources I have presented and do some research of your own. And don't spread unfounded rumors as historical fact, there's too much of that going around already.<br /> <br /> Back on topic. I actually like your ideas about the stories of changelings based on fairy-tales coming face to face with an origin that is...lacking in the charms of the popular version. It's a cool idea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11313-thunderwheel","user":"Thunderwheel","date":". 04-30-2017, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11313-thunderwheel","name":"Thunderwheel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T12:52:40-07:00","id":1085855,"title":"","content":"What are some of your core sources? I am curious to learn more about your background and research. I enjoy exploring several different sources on a subject even if they contradict each other. My professors at college would metaphorically beat each other bloody over views on a curriculum subject<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>Note: To justify the existence of Robin Hood, Manchester cites a grave marker.</i><br /> <br /> Also, thank you for complementing my ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T12:53:55-07:00","id":1085857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thunderwheel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1085689#post1085689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am a professional researcher and scholar. I take information from disparate sources, including archaeological work and written documents, and interpret them to create a cohesive story that helps to contextualize the past. I frequently use speculation to fill in gaps in the historical record, and when I do, I explicitly say so. And when I say something based on someone else's work, I cite it, so that other people can go to the source, verify, and make a judgement as to whether my interpretations are valid.<br /> <br /> I am not a German historian, but that's irrelevant because I don't have to be. Scholarship isn't just making stuff up; citing sources is a basic tenet of good scholarship. A little bit of quick internet research on the &quot;real&quot; story of the Pied Piper yields lots of results. Look at some of them, and pay special attention to the ones that give sources, like this one:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.medievalists.net/2014/12/pied-piper-hamelin-medieval-mass-abduction/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.medievalists.net/2014/12/...ass-abduction/</a><br /> <br /> There's a theme here. These people say that it isn't clear what the historical event that spawned the Piper story was, and they don't know because the sources are unclear (but none cited ever mention children's bodies). You called me out for &quot;only citing one source,&quot; but that source cited several, and Manchester didn't cite one at all. That makes his version unreliable. Note that that's not the same as 'false.' But if he doesn't cite a source, and lots of other folks cite sources that don't support his story....well then.<br /> <br /> It is completely fair to call Manchester a mediocre scholar. It's even fair to call him a poor one, because HE MAKES UN-SOURCED STATEMENTS AND PRESENTS THEM AS FACT. Other actual scholars of the region and period have commented on his shortcomings, reviews are available to the searcher. So you see, I'm not calling him mediocre because I disagree with him. I'm calling him mediocre because he's mediocre, and I presented an argument backed by evidence. Up to the reader to judge if it's valid, but do me the courtesy of not disagreeing with me just because you don't like what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> This will be the last time I post on the subject, because I have nothing further to add to my stance on the issue and this is a sideline from the topic. But since you called me out on my background before you'd consider my position, ask yourself this:<br /> <br /> Why are you so convinced Manchester is correct? Have you done research that supports his theory? If so, by all means, publish it, it would be a significant contribution to German historical scholarship. If not, then if you you want to know the &quot;truth&quot; about these things, start with the sources I have presented and do some research of your own. And don't spread unfounded rumors as historical fact, there's too much of that going around already.<br /> <br /> Back on topic. I actually like your ideas about the stories of changelings based on fairy-tales coming face to face with an origin that is...lacking in the charms of the popular version. It's a cool idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have any fairy tale character you would recommend being reinterpreted into word 10 Changelings? I would like to hear your ideas on this<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T13:40:28-07:00","id":1085872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1055953-legendary-epic-changeling?p=1072516#post1072516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fully support giving more attention to the less known myths and fables.<br /> <br /> Also, why not go beyond just listing Kiths, Seemings and powers? I think we can do better. How about we focus on how the tales of these characters change over time? Some of these characters might still be alive (or have heirs/disciples/descendants). They probably have a thing or two to say about the stories we have been telling about them. In other cases, changelings of today might take on their classic roles, but with modern sensibilities, often becoming Grimms and/or joining appropriate Courts. What happens when these two meet each other? Can the old and new tales co-exist?</div> </div> </div> </div>Another thing that would be interesting to explore with a changeling who is older than 100 years old is old values clashing with modern values. I believe that while our opinions change, our core values tend to be concrete by our mid twenties. Up until recently in human history (around 1950 I believe) people did not enjoy the material wealth we do today, death by violence and disease was common place, marriages were arranged for material benefits, and many people lived in a religious fog. I believe that changelings who grew up before the nineteen forties would clash with our modern values and technology (I am seeing this with my grandparents).<br /> <br /> This would especially be interesting to explore with a word 10 changeling who is several hundred years old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T21:17:29-07:00","id":1086052,"title":"","content":"This Monster would make a fun word 10 changeling.<br /> <span style=\"color:#211B14\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Black Annis </b>(also known as <b>Black Agnes</b>) is a witch and boogeyman figure in English folklore dating back to the eighteenth-century.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">It is said that she haunts the countryside of Leicestershire, living in a dark cave located somewhere in the Dane Hills, known as &quot;Black Annis' Bower&quot; by locals, with an old oak tree marking the entrance, a tree she often hid in waiting for someone to snatch up.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">She was said to be very tall and horrible, with blue skin, glowing eyes, long, sharp teeth and claw-like fingers, which she used to tear into the small children she prepared to eat.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">After she had eaten the child, she hung their skin on the old oak tree to dry, later to be sewn in her skirt made purely of child skin.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The hag only left the cave at dark, where she set off to find tasty children, the tastiest being those who misbehaved. She also fed on farm animals, like sheep and lamb, much to the local farmers' disdain.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Children were warned not to venture into the Dane Hills alone, lest they run into Black Annis and be snatched away into her Bower to be sucked dry.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">It was most common to see her long, bony arms pulling children through shack windows, as glass was not put in place during the eighteenth-century.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The witch's horrible howl could be heard from miles away, giving time to prepare for her visit. It is said that you could even hear her sharp teeth grinding together if you listened.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Her cave was filled with dirt late into the nineteenth-century, possibly literally burying Black Annis forever. A housing estate now stands on the grounds of the old crone's lair.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T17:02:36-07:00","id":1086385,"title":"","content":"Here are two goddesses/spirits that would make interesting wyrd 10 changelings.<br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><i>Berchta</i></b>, also called <b><i>Perchta</i></b>, is a goddess of southern Germany and Austria who later became known in folklore as a kind of boogeyman who would frighten children. Modern Heathens look to a variety of sources to understand her as a goddess and so the understandings of her can vary widely.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> In modern folklore Berchta/Perchta is seen as a lesser spirit who punishes miscreants and who has an assortment of fairy beings called Perchten who travel with her. Perchten is also a word used to describe masks worn during processions, called Perchtenl\u00e4ufe, to drive out evil spirits. These masks are made of a variety of material and usually take the form of grotesque animals; they appear in two styles, schiachperchten (ugly perchten) and sch\u00f6nperchten (beautiful perchten). Ugly perchten drive out evil spirits while beautiful perchten bring luck. The ugly perchten are also associated with the Krampus traditions in modern times as the masks are reminiscent of the appearance of Krampus.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> In the older material she was almost certainly a goddess, similar in many ways to Frau Holda; in fact some people believe the two are the same being under different names. Berchta appears in those areas of Germany where Holda does not lending some credence to this idea, and the two are both associated with the Wild Hunt and caring for the souls of dead children. Both are also associated with Yule and with spinning and also have in their retinue fairy beings - perchten with Perchta (Berchta) and huldufolk with Holda. Both Holda and Berchta are also associated with the wagon and the plow and both are associated with witches. However there are notable differences as well, and these are enough to persuade me that the two are separate, albeit likely related, beings. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Berchta's name means bright, luminous and it is said she appears dressed in white. Berchta received offerings on rooftops and she is associated with specific foods. Grimm discusses a fish and dumpling dish as well as oatmeal dish connected to Berchta, which her followers would eat on the last night of Yule (Grimm gives her feast day as either December 25th or January 6th; in modern practice it is usually December 31st); those who failed to observe this practice were severely punished. Berchta was also strongly connected to iron and said to have a nose made of this metal. In many of Berchta's stories she is said to be accompanied by either the fey perchten or by the ghosts of young children called heimchen (literally &quot;crickets&quot;), which she cares for; these spirits are said to bring rain to the earth while she tends her own realm, or as Grimm says &quot;while she worked underground with her plough&quot;. Besides being associated with agriculture Berchta is also associated at least tentatively with streams and rivers, as in one story where she sets an arrogant woman to spinning and the resulting thread on its spools is thrown into a stream to give it back to Berhcta. Berchta is known to reward those who help her, usually by giving them the archetypal fairy gift of a useless seeming object - in this case wood chips - which turn to gold. She also punishes those who offend her, typically by cutting them open and stuffing their body with straw, although in some stories she forces them to spin, blinds them, or, as in one tale from Bavaria, she hits a greedy man with an ax (Grimm, 1888). In older material she is described as gentle and generous, a kind Goddess who appears clad in white to care for babies while the adults sleep; indeed Grimm calls her &quot;the White Lady&quot;.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Some people believe that Berchta evolved from the older Germano-Gaulish goddess Bricta (Brixta) who was a goddess of healing. Bricta was known in Luxeuil France, not too far from the border of what is now south western Germany. Bricta may mean either &quot;shining one&quot; or &quot;magic, enchantment&quot; and she was associated with both healing and cursing, and possibly with the river Breuchin which might be named after her. This means that not only are the names possibly connected in their meanings but both also have connections to water, specifically streams or rivers. If we give weight to this idea then Berchta could also be seen as a healing Goddess in a German heathen context.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Holda is a Germanic goddess with many interesting characteristics \u2013 maiden, mother, hag, spinner, stormbringer, ruler of the Wild Hunt, protector and thief of children\u2019s souls. She was usually seen dressed in snow-white with white or silver hair, regardless of whether she appears as young and beautiful or as an old hag. In this latter form, she is said to have crooked teeth, a big nose, and one foot flatter than the other from working the spinning wheel. She wears keys at her belt, the sign of the lady of the house.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">First, she is a goddess of the domestic arts \u2013 spinning, cooking, cleaning, and child care. She is a patroness of housewives, and what she values above all is industriousness. There are many legends of her rewarding diligent female workers and punishing lazy ones. She would rock cradles while exhausted mothers slept. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Her preference for hard workers is reflected in the German folktale of \u201cFrau Holle\u201d, where a young girl falls down the well into a strange underworld. She helps every creature she meets, and willingly cleans for the old woman in her cottage, after which the old woman sends her back with a gift \u2013 a gold piece falls from her lips every time she speaks. Her mother, amazed, forces her lazy sister down the well; the sister refuses to help anyone and the old woman sends her back with a different gift \u2013 instead of gold, toads drop from her lips when she says anything.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">She was especially stern when it came to women who were lazy about spinning, which was her specialty - particularly the spinning of flax. One legend has a peasant man stumbling into a cave in a mountain where Holda is seated enthroned with maidens clustered about her. She offers to give the dazed man a gift; humbly, he asks for the cluster of blue flowers in her hand. These were the flowers of flax, which according to the tale was unknown in that area at the time. Holda gave the man some flaxseeds, and eventually taught his wife to ret, scotch, break, and spin flax, thus giving us a myth about the beginning of flax culture. Holda was implacable about using her gift properly; hard workers who fell asleep over their work would awake to find their spinning done for them, while lazy women would find their spindles broken or burned.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">She was also a protectress of children, although some of her myths might seem quite the opposite at first glance. It was said that Holda collected the souls of dead children, usually infants who died too soon \u2013 before being christened in Christian times, before being named in the days before that. In pre-Christian times, children were named at nine days old, and before that were believed not to be attached to the ancestral tree. If they died before that time, Holda would take them on instead of their ancestors. She also took children of other ages, for various reasons. The darker side of her myth had her stealing the lives of otherwise healthy children. She was said to travel as an old woman in a wagon, flanked by a procession of childrens\u2019 dead souls.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T22:23:51-07:00","id":1088108,"title":"","content":"In an Epic/Legendary core book, one theme I think it should explore is how to play wyrd 10 changelings as pagan gods or divine spirits. I don't just mean that they have cults that worship them, but through their high wyrd and court mantle, are actually able to control/ influence the destiny of the mortal realm to a certain degree. I can see this happening by being bound to certain festivals/pagan holidays.<br /> <br /> For example, <i><b>Perchta</b></i> and <i><b>Holda </b></i>are associated with Christmas. I can see there being a entitlement made of Monsters, Demons, and Spirits associated with Christmas and can influence the mortal realm during the Christmas night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}